326	     * Normalize the owner's supplied address into its canonical stored form and report whether an
327	     * address was supplied at all. The owner may supply its address either as the structured
328	     * {@code addressLine1}/{@code addressLine2} fields or as the flat {@code address} field, which is
329	     * kept for backward compatibility; the structured form is preferred whenever a non-blank
330	     * {@code addressLine1} is present. Each supplied field is run through the {@link AddressNormalizer}
331	     * (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, common street-type abbreviations expanded). When the
332	     * structured form is used, the normalized {@code addressLine1} and {@code addressLine2} are stored
333	     * back and the composed {@link Owner#getAddress() address} becomes the normalized
334	     * {@code addressLine1} with a single space and the normalized {@code addressLine2} appended when an
335	     * {@code addressLine2} is present; when the flat form is used, the normalized flat address is
336	     * stored and no structured lines are kept. Returns {@code true} once a non-blank address has been
337	     * normalized and stored, or {@code false} when neither form supplied an address, in which case the
338	     * create must be rejected with {@code 400 Bad Request}.
